class.description:
A [DataSchema] is an ordered list of [DataField]s that describes the keys, columns or attributes of a data file, independent of its format: [CSV], [INI], [JSON], [TOML], [YAML] and [XML]. [method validate] checks parsed data and returns a [DataValidation] with every issue and its position. Save a schema as a [code].tres[/code] file and edit it in the inspector, or create one in code with [method create_from_dictionary].
[method validate] understands three shapes of data: a [Dictionary] (fields by key, such as a JSON object or the sections of an [INI] file), an [Array] of [Dictionary] records (such as a JSON array; the index is the issue row) and an [Array] of rows ([PackedStringArray], fields by position). [method TextDataFormat.validate] validates the data of a format resource and adds lines; [CSV] matches its columns to the fields by header name.
Nested data is validated through [member DataField.schema] ([Dictionary] values) and [member DataField.element_schema] or [member DataField.element_type] ([Array] values), at any depth.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var schema = DataSchema.create_from_dictionary({
	"id": TYPE_INT,
	"name": TYPE_STRING,
	"stats": { "attack": TYPE_INT },
	"tags": [TYPE_STRING],
})
schema.get_field("id").unique = true

var result = schema.validate(JSON.parse_string(FileAccess.get_file_as_string("res://data/items.json")))
for i in result.get_issue_count():
	print("%s: %s" % [result.get_issue_path(i), result.get_issue_message(i)])
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var schema = DataSchema.CreateFromDictionary(new Godot.Collections.Dictionary
{
	{ "id", (int)Variant.Type.Int },
	{ "name", (int)Variant.Type.String },
	{ "stats", new Godot.Collections.Dictionary { { "attack", (int)Variant.Type.Int } } },
	{ "tags", new Godot.Collections.Array { (int)Variant.Type.String } },
});
schema.GetField("id").Unique = true;

DataValidation result = schema.Validate(Json.ParseString(FileAccess.GetFileAsString("res://data/items.json")));
for (int i = 0; i < result.GetIssueCount(); i++)
{
	GD.Print($"{result.GetIssuePath(i)}: {result.GetIssueMessage(i)}");
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
Validation is explicit: nothing is validated on load or when data changes.
[b]Note:[/b] Validation only reads the schema, so it can run on any thread while the schema is not changed.
